<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="d1557cfa">&lt;p&gt;
    Receive feedback from the project team on how well the project was executed and begin to document lessons learned
    (e.g., what worked well and why, what did not work well and why, what could have been done differently, and what to
    leverage going forward). This meeting can be conducted with either the client or the project team depending on the type
    of engagement. Elements of a good team debrief meeting include honesty and an opportunity to allow the team to provide
    project reflections and suggestions. The discussion areas will contribute to lessons learned and should address project
    aspects such as mobilization, communications, planning, quality, resourcing, teaming, etc.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The general steps to consider include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Conduct team debrief session
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Capture lessons learned&amp;nbsp;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Update lessons learned log/document
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Review lessons learned with team for clarification and revisions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Finalize lessons learned document
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify project resources to be released from project assignments
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify resource management that resource assignments are complete with project work
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Notify project resources that they have been released from the project
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Release resources from project once feedback is documented.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
